---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Our Business Model"
  description="How BeekeeperML stays free for home lab users and how we plan to sustain it."
>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="page-inner">
      <h1>Our Business Model</h1>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Free forever for home lab users</h2>
        <p>
	If you're running BeekeeperML on your own server for personal or educational work, it's free forever.
        </p>
	<p>My goal with this project was to make something for my own small home lab, to make my personal RL/ML projects easier. If Beekeeper helps you as a student, hobbyist, or independent researcher, please consider it my gift to you, and a very small contribution to moving human knowledge forward.  
	</p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
	<h2>How I plan to make money</h2>
	<p>Unfortunately this project does eventually need to make money if I'm going to keep supporting it and adding features. Methods I'm exploring: </p>
	<ul>
		<li>Backend Integrations - As BeekeeperML adds support for cloud compute providers, I'm looking at ways to earn a referral cut on compute spend that flows through the platform. This would effectively be free for you as a user, while supporting the project</li>
		<li>Enterprise Support - Businesses with over $1 Million in annual revenue don't fit the "personal project" description, and should reach out to discuss licensing before use.</li>
	</ul>

      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>License model</h2>
        <p>
          BeekeeperML is source-available under the <strong>Business Source License 1.1 (BUSL)</strong>.
          The source code is public and you can read, modify, and run it — the license just defines
          the terms under which you can do so commercially.
        </p>
        <p>
          Personal, educational, and non-commercial home lab use is permitted without restriction.
          Organizations with over $1 million in annual revenue, or anyone offering BeekeeperML
          to third parties on a hosted or embedded basis, must reach out to discuss a commercial license.
        </p>

      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
	For all inquiries, contact robert.cowher@beekeeperml.dev
	</p>

      </section>


    </div>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  .page-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 3rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .section p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .section ul {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .section li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .section li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
